TABS (tmux windows) for the pane-of-glass. tmux windows ARE tabs — a session holds many windows, each a full-screen frame, with a tab strip in the status bar; conductor drives them prefix-free (new-window/select-window/rename-window/move-window), human switches with Ctrl-b 0/1/n/p. Verified live 2026-08-03: added tabs without stealing focus (-d), swapped a live keeper (ubersitrep) into its own tab via cross-window join-pane, registry-by-name survived the move. GOTCHA found same day: the status bar (the tab strip) was `status off` on the attached CLIENT even though global was on — no bar, no visible tabs; `tmux set-option -t <sess> status on` fixes it (costs 1 row). Fits the design: the CLAUDE.md line 'builders stay in their own window' literally means a separate tab. Three candidate models (Peter: explore later, not committing yet): (1) PANE-0 + BUILDERS — tab0 holds the keeper pane arrangement, extra tabs hold builder sessions, tabs become the keeper/builder boundary; (2) PANE-0 + FOCUS TABS — pop any keeper full-screen into its own transient tab to focus, close to return; (3) GROUPED PANE-0s — several themed tabs of keeper arrangements (astro / infra / web), overview spans all. Overview would want a per-tab summary or an all-tabs headline. NAMING: do NOT call any of this a "cockpit" (Peter rejected the term 2026-08-03) — it's pane 0 / tab 0.
